---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import {groups,resources} from '../../data/researchResources';
const roles=[
['Taxonomist','What is it, and what distinguishes it?','Identifies, describes, compares and circumscribes taxa using morphology, molecules, ecology and other evidence.'],
['Systematist','How does it fit into the diversity of life?','Studies organismal diversity, relationships and classification; often combines taxonomy with evolutionary evidence.'],
['Phylogeneticist','What are its evolutionary relationships?','Infers evolutionary trees from molecular or other characters, with explicit models, sampling and uncertainty.'],
['Nomenclature specialist','Which name can we correctly use?','Interprets the naming Code, publication history, typification, priority and legitimacy. Sometimes called a nomenclaturalist.'],
['Fungal ecologist','Where does it live and what does it do?','Investigates habitat, substrate, hosts, symbioses, interactions, distributions and ecosystem processes.'],
['Collection curator','Can another researcher check the evidence?','Preserves, documents and makes specimens or cultures discoverable for future comparisons.']
];
---
<Base title="Research Resources | MycoGeeky">
<section class="page-hero container"><p class="eyebrow">INVESTIGATE / RESEARCH RESOURCES</p><h1>Follow the evidence. Find the tools.</h1><p class="lead">A field guide to the research ecosystem behind fungal names, specimens, sequences and scientific discoveries. You don't need a degree to start exploring it.</p><p class="resource-count">{resources.length} resources across {groups.length} research areas · <a href="#directory">Browse the directory ↓</a></p></section>
<section class="section soft"><div class="container"><p class="eyebrow">WHO DOES WHAT?</p><h2>Six ways to ask a better question.</h2><p class="resource-intro">These aren't rigid job titles. Many researchers do several kinds of work—and the same mushroom may need all of them.</p><div class="resource-roles">{roles.map(([title,question,description])=><article class="resource-role"><h3>{title}</h3><p class="resource-question">{question}</p><p>{description}</p></article>)}</div><p class="resource-footnote">A phylogenetic tree may support a lineage, but it doesn't automatically create a species name. Taxonomic judgments and nomenclatural rules answer different questions.</p></div></section>
<section class="section" id="directory"><div class="container"><p class="eyebrow">THE RESEARCH DIRECTORY</p><h2>What are you trying to find out?</h2><p class="resource-intro">Browse by research area. Each entry explains what it can do and one limitation worth remembering.</p><nav class="resource-nav" aria-label="Research resource categories"><a href="#names">Names</a><a href="#specimens">Specimens</a><a href="#sequence">DNA & trees</a><a href="#field">Ecology</a><a href="#literature">Literature</a></nav>{groups.map(group=><section class="resource-group" id={group.id}><div class="resource-group-head"><h3>{group.title}</h3><p>{group.intro}</p></div><div class="resource-cards">{group.resources.map(([name,url,purpose,note,source])=><article class="resource-entry"><div class="resource-entry-top"><h4><a href={url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{name} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></h4><span class="resource-origin">{source==='paper'?'In the paper':'Additional'}</span></div><p>{purpose}</p><p class="resource-caution"><strong>Keep in mind:</strong> {note}</p></article>)}</div></section>)}</div></section>
<section class="section soft"><div class="container"><p class="eyebrow">START WITH THE SOURCE</p><h2>A practical guide to describing new fungal species.</h2><p class="resource-intro">This directory began with Aime and colleagues' 2021 guide, <em>How to publish a new fungal species, or name, version 3.0</em>. The paper distinguishes the formal requirements of nomenclature from taxonomic best practices, and its page 10 checklist follows the path from specimen and evidence to publication and repository updates.</p><p>Some resources above are named in that paper; others are additions for broader research workflows. The paper is from 2021, so always consult current software documentation, database policies and the current nomenclatural Code.</p><a class="button primary" href="https://doi.org/10.1186/s43008-021-00063-1" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read the open-access paper ↗</a></div></section>
</Base>
